        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): add board filter to workboard toolbar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #101789: Adds a \"Board\" dropdown filter to the /workboard toolbar so cards can be scoped to a single board, following the existing agent-filter pattern.\n\nWorkboard supports multiple named boards (`workboard_boards`, `boardId` on cards, `workboard dispatch --board`), but teams running more than one active board had no way in the Control UI to filter the visible card list down to one board.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a `boardFilter` to the workboard UI state, filter chain, and toolbar alongside the existing agent/priority/status filters:\n\n- **`matchesBoardFilter`** — filters cards by `metadata.automation.boardId`, with \"all\", \"none\" (no board), and per-board options\n- **`buildBoardFilterOptions`** — derives board options from boards present across loaded cards\n- **Toolbar select** — rendered between priority and agent filters, only shown when boards exist\n- **State** — persisted in `WorkboardUiState.boardFilter`, normalized on render\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Operators can scope the Kanban view to a single board\n- Board dropdown only appears when cards have board IDs (no noise for single-board deployments)\n- Follows the same interaction pattern as the existing agent filter\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [x] `pnpm test ui/src/pages/workboard/view.test.ts` — 69 tests pass\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "feat/101789-workboard-board-filter",
